{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4c7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f78-0ca7-7650-b043-6178918d4030"},"sequence":190,"recorded_at":1780531400000375,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"09066c51-cf5e-4ab0-8fb1-8339d1838d54","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"09066c51-cf5e-4ab0-8fb1-8339d1838d54","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"09066c51-cf5e-4ab0-8fb1-8339d1838d54"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"f4076d97-fab6-4ab9-b9ac-71e991cd809b"},"task_id":"f4076d97-fab6-4ab9-b9ac-71e991cd809b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"f4076d97-fab6-4ab9-b9ac-71e991cd809b","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/verdict.md`.\n1|# Review verdict: TASK-260903-2qgu2p — specify-landing-ownership-and-modes (revision 4)\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260904-5fdc6b (reviewer archetype). Change Request\n4|`CR-TASK-260903-2qgu2p-4` revision 4, base `41ef87e7`, candidate tree\n5|`c59c58ff` (identical to base), `repository_delta=empty`.\n6|Evidence gathered read-only in the Story worktree and the control root at\n7|`41ef87e7` = fetched `origin/main` = story branch tip. Probes: `git`,\n8|`gh issue view`, python over `.temp/changerequests` (all 125 recorded\n9|revisions) and `.temp/integration-txn`, `sed`/`grep` over `tools/board-cli`,\n10|`references/`, `.roles/` and `AGENTS.md`. Nothing modified.\n11|\n12|## Verdict: ACCEPTED\n13|\n14|Both findings of the previous verdict (RUN-260904-0239f6) are closed, and I\n15|closed them by re-measuring the specified predicate myself rather than reading\n16|the producer's numbers. All five rework demands were delivered.\n17|\n18|---\n19|\n20|## Why an empty repository delta is the right outcome here\n21|\n22|The brief's section 6 forbids implementing the landing change and modifying\n23|product code, configuration or the skill; the acceptance criteria end with the\n24|same prohibition. Every deliverable of this leaf — board elements, a GitHub\n25|issue, outcome resources — lives outside the working tree. A non-empty delta\n26|would have been a finding *against* the producer.\n27|`git diff 41ef87e7 c59c58ff` is empty and `git status --short` in the worktree\n28|is empty. Correct outcome for this leaf. The verdict below is about the content\n29|of `TASK-260903-1l4qu5`, which is where this leaf's work product actually is.\n30|\n31|---\n32|\n33|## 1. Finding 1 (predicate refuses ordinary work): CLOSED, independently measured\n34|\n35|The base-relative `R = rev-list B..S` form is gone. The specified predicate is\n36|now: refuse iff `repository_delta` is present AND some commit `X` exists that is\n37|an ancestor of the freshly fetched `T`, is not in the Story's covering set `N`,\n38|and whose tree equals the revision's recorded `candidate_tree_oid`. No base and\n39|no branch tip enter it.\n40|\n41|I implemented that predicate from the element text alone (`/tmp/rev_probe.py`,\n42|scratch, not in the repo) and ran it over live state at\n43|`T = origin/main = 41ef87e7` (505 trunk ancestors), with `N` built from\n44|`.temp/integration-txn` as specified (`rev-list expected_trunk_oid..candidate_commit_oid`,\n45|records with no `candidate_commit_oid` contributing nothing):\n46|\n47|| Population | Producer claims | I measured | Held |\n48||---|---|---|---|\n49|| Recorded revisions | 124 (59 story_final / 65 task_delta) | **125** (59 / 66) — the extra is rev4 itself, created after their probe | Yes |\n50|| `repository_delta` present / empty | 92 / 32 | **92 / 33** (same +1) | Yes |\n51|| Revisions missing `candidate_tree_oid` or `repository_delta` | 0 of 124 | **0 of 125** | Yes |\n52|| New predicate fires, all revisions | exactly 1 | **exactly 1**: `CR-BUG-260903-3lcta8-1` → `a64536a2dc79…` | Yes |\n53|| Current `ready`/`accepted` revisions | 24 | **24** (14 ready + 10 accepted over 47 elements) | Yes |\n54|| …of which present / empty | 17 / 7 | **17 / 7**, same seven ids | Yes |\n55|| New predicate fires, current set | 1, the 09-03 true positive | **1**, `CR-BUG-260903-3lcta8-1` | Yes |\n56|| False positives | 0 | **0** | Yes |\n57|\n58|The five false refuses the previous verdict reproduced (`1klgdm-6`, `6hey5j-2`,\n59|`a9jtwd-1`, `12kn9a-4` plus the one true positive) are gone: the refreshed-base\n60|shape cannot reach this predicate because no base and no tip is read.\n61|`CR-BUG-260903-a9jtwd-1` — this task's own parent design, the case the previous\n62|verdict used as the sharpest instance — admits.\n63|\n64|### The empty-delta exemption is load-bearing, not a convenience hole\n65|\n66|The element exempts `repository_delta=empty` on the argument that `C` equals the\n67|base tree by construction. I checked both halves rather than accepting either:\n68|\n69|- **The invariant holds:** over all **33** empty-delta revisions,\n70|  `candidate_tree_oid == base_tree_oid` in **33 of 33**. Zero counterexamples.\n71|- **Without the exemption the gate would false-refuse 24 of those 33.** I ran\n72|  the predicate with the exemption removed: 24 empty-delta revisions have a tree\n73|  matching a non-`N` trunk ancestor, because their base *is* a trunk commit.\n74|\n75|So the exemption is what keeps the gate from re-committing the exact sin the\n76|previous verdict blocked on, and the element pays for it honestly by naming the\n77|resulting evasion (committed-then-pushed branch head) as a stated bound rather\n78|than claiming cover.\n79|\n80|## 2. Finding 2 (vacuous at task_delta publish): CLOSED structurally\n81|\n82|The vacuousness came from `B == S` at publish for `task_delta`\n83|(`currentBranchOID`, `internal/spawnruntime/changerequest.go:884-893`, bound at\n84|`:550`). The new predicate reads no base at all, so the kind-dependent base\n85|derivation is irrelevant to whether it can fire. Coverage is stated as a measured\n86|ratio (92/124 overall, 17/24 current, both kinds, both entry points) with the\n87|empty-delta bound named at 7/24 and 32/124, and residual bound R1\n88|(push-then-supersede) named as outside the threat model. My independent counts\n89|agree on every one of those numbers.\n90|\n91|## 3. Every code site the element names, verified to exist and to say what it claims\n92|\n93|| Element's claim | Site | Result |\n94||---|---|---|\n95|| Publish path creates the record at `store.Create` | `internal/spawnruntime/changerequest.go:167` (inside `fileChangeRequests.Publish`) | Held |\n96|| Production publish entry point | `(*Runtime).publishChangeRequestForProducer` at `:464` | Held (a method, hence invisible to a `func name` grep) |\n97|| story_final base from `convergeStoryFinalBaseAuthority` | `:647` | Held |\n98|| task_delta base from `currentBranchOID` | `:884` | Held |\n99|| `ResolveConfiguredProtectedAuthority` exists to add at publish | `internal/worktree/trunk.go:255` | Held |\n100|| Accept resolves fresh authority | `internal/changerequest/accept.go:64` `Store.Accept` → `resolveReviewedTrunk:107` → `ResolveConfiguredProtectedAuthority` | Held, **with a qualification, see observation 1** |\n101|| `IsAncestorOfTrunk`, `ResolveRef` helpers exist | `changerequest/basis.go:72`, `changerequest/git.go:160` | Held |\n102|| Txn phase ladder is monotonic so \"or later\" is well-defined | `internal/integration/txn.go:26-51`, `phaseOrder :58-68` | Held. `transition_refused` (4) and `integration_abandoned` (5) sort after `git_integrated_board_pending` (2) and are reached only after trunk advanced, so including them in `N` is correct, not an accident |\n103|| Prompt line lost to `AGENTS.md` | `cmd/spawn_workspace.go:554` | Held verbatim |\n104|| `worktree --help` assumes a remote named origin | `cmd/worktree.go:30` | Held verbatim |\n105|| statuses.md embeds this repo's commit-time prose | `references/statuses.md:374` (\"the previous day at 20:01 MSK\") | Held |\n106|| \"commit-owning mover's own call\" | `references/tracked-background-spawn.md:209` | Held |\n107|| Stale `validation_not_configured` bullet in both role bodies | `.roles/orchestrator/role.md:86`, `.roles/coordinator/role.md:68` | Held (element says \"line 86 in each\"; coordinator is 68 — the criterion is text-based, so this is cosmetic) |\n108|| `AGENTS.md` lifecycle bullet, Landing Flow, `agent-session-manager` coupling | `AGENTS.md:43`, `:50`, `:52` | Held, all three |\n109|\n110|AC 2's grep guard is non-vacuous today: `20:01 MSK` and `refs/remotes/origin/HEAD`\n111|are both live in the named surfaces, so the guard is red before the work and\n112|green after.\n113|\n114|## 4. Attacks on the mutant set\n115|\n116|- **Removing `N`** (refuse even for ladder-landed work) is caught by admit\n117|  fixture (d).\n118|- **Narrowing `N`** to the bare `candidate_commit_oid` set is caught by the\n119|  mandated N-disposition fixture.\n120|- **Removing the empty-delta exemption** is caught by admit fixtures (a) and (b)\n121|  — and my measurement says it would fail on 24 live shapes, so the fixture is\n122|  representative, not contrived.\n123|- **Reverting to the base-relative form** is caught by admit fixture (e), the\n124|  refreshed-base shape, modelled on the two live CRs the previous verdict used.\n125|- **Widening to bare tip ancestry** is caught by admit fixture (a).\n126|- **Deleting the call site** is caught, but that mutant is delete-only and proves\n127|  only presence; the three separating mutants above carry the bound. See\n128|  observation 2 for the one direction they do not separate.\n129|\n130|## Observations carried forward to the `TASK-260903-1l4qu5` implementer, none blocking\n131|\n132|1. **`resolveReviewedTrunk` runs only for `story_final`.** `Store.Accept`\n133|   (`accept.go:79-85`) calls it under `if current.Kind == KindStoryFinal`. The\n134|   element's sentence \"at accept_cr, T is already freshly resolved by\n135|   `resolveReviewedTrunk`; evaluate the detector after it\" is therefore true for\n136|   `story_final` and false for `task_delta`, which resolves no protected\n137|   authority on the accept path today. The implementer must add the same fresh\n138|   read there that the element already adds at publish. This cannot ship\n139|   silently: AC 6 mandates a refuse fixture for \"the same publish-plus-accept\n140|   pair for a `task_delta` candidate\", which fails until the read exists. Prose\n141|   imprecision over a falsifiable criterion, not a hole — but fix the sentence\n142|   while implementing.\n143|2. **No mutant separates \"any ancestor of T\" from \"the tip of T\".** All three\n144|   separating mutants widen the refusal. An implementation that checked only\n145|   whether `tree(T) == C` would pass every fixture as specified, and would still\n146|   catch the 09-03 shape at the moment of the push while silently admitting it\n147|   one trunk commit later. Build the refuse fixtures with at least one commit on\n148|   the fixture protected ref *after* the out-of-band push, and add the tip-only\n149|   narrowing mutant.\n150|3. **Content equality is not causation.** A candidate that reverts trunk to an\n151|   earlier state produces a tree equal to an older trunk commit's tree and would\n152|   refuse `change_request_landed_out_of_band` naming a commit it never published.\n153|   Zero occurrences across all 125 live revisions, the direction fails closed\n154|   with a full packet, and the element's threat model is accidental landing\n155|   through a documented flow — so this is a bound to name alongside R1, not a\n156|   defect to fix.\n157|\n158|## Definition of Done check\n159|\n160|| Item | Result |\n161||---|---|\n162|| Accepted design and its review verdict read in full; elements stand alone | Yes |\n163|| Explicit precedence for trunk ownership, with override clause | Yes |\n164|| Protocol dependence on a per-team instruction file identified and removed | Yes — eight sites, each verified to exist at the line named; `AGENTS.md` reduced to a pointer |\n165|| Local-only landing defined and reconciled with Concept A | Yes (`TASK-260903-9w5nue`) |\n166|| Collaborative landing, remote rejection as CAS, local trunk as replication | Yes |\n167|| Mode signal deterministic, tool-readable, fail-closed | Yes |\n168|| Concepts A and B restated as implementable requirements | Yes |\n169|| Manual commit-time conflict resolved | Yes (`TASK-260903-2e8rws`) |\n170|| One task or several, with order and blocking edges | Yes — four tasks, edges reciprocal (`2xw0ar` blocked by all three; verified in both directions) |\n171|| Board elements with description, AC, checklist, estimate, task class, review policy | Yes — `1l4qu5` fib 5, `9w5nue` fib 13, `2e8rws` fib 3, `2xw0ar` fib 8; all `code`/`required` |\n172|| GitHub issue with the board identifier in the body | Yes — #117 OPEN, nine board ids as literal text |\n173|| Outcome resource recording what, why, and questions decided | Yes — `_rework-rev4.md`, five questions decided |\n174|| No product code, configuration or skill file modified | Yes — empty delta, clean worktree |\n175|| **Gates attacked, not read; positive-path-only evidence not accepted** | **Yes** — the predicate was re-implemented from the element text and run over all 125 live revisions (1 fire, 0 false positives), the exemption invariant checked on 33 of 33 and its necessity measured at 24 of 33, and the mutant set attacked in both directions |\n176|\n177|## Rework demands from RUN-260904-0239f6\n178|\n179|| Demand | Result |\n180||---|---|\n181|| 1. Predicate meaning \"content this candidate produced reached trunk\", measured, counts recorded in the element | Done; counts recorded and independently reproduced |\n182|| 2. Coverage as a measured ratio with named bounds per kind and entry point | Done; 92/124, 17/24, empty-delta bound 7/24 and 32/124, R1 named |\n183|| 3. Admit fixture (e) for the refreshed-base shape plus a separating mutant | Done, at both entry points, with the rev-list-form revert mutant |\n184|| 4. Refuse fixture driven through the production publish path, no hand-written `base_oid` | Done for both kinds at both entry points, production sites named and verified real |\n185|| 5. One-line disposition of `N`'s two readings | Done — wide reading adopted, narrow rejected with reason, narrowing mutant mandated |\n186|\n187|## Disposition\n188|\n189|`accept_cr(TASK-260903-2qgu2p, revision=4, evidence=TASK-260903-2qgu2p_review-verdict.md)`.\n190|The element parks at `to-review` as the accepted handoff; the orchestrator owns\n191|the `done` transition with `commit_ack`. No `commit_ack` supplied here."}}}
