{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7fb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f78-0ca7-7650-b043-6178918d4030"},"sequence":600,"recorded_at":1780531400001195,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"09066c51-cf5e-4ab0-8fb1-8339d1838d54","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"09066c51-cf5e-4ab0-8fb1-8339d1838d54","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"09066c51-cf5e-4ab0-8fb1-8339d1838d54"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"b1db029f-1aea-4950-9827-cf91af3c7a9b"},"task_id":"b1db029f-1aea-4950-9827-cf91af3c7a9b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"b1db029f-1aea-4950-9827-cf91af3c7a9b","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1939 line(s) above)\n1940|that a claimed clause is a real obligation of the claimed section, that it is\n1941|quoted verbatim at the line it occupies, that the discharging acceptance case is\n1942|registered and owned by the binding, and that the declared level equals the\n1943|measured ratio. **It cannot decide that the named acceptance case exercises the\n1944|clause's meaning.** A binding could enumerate every clause of a section and\n1945|point all of them at one weak test, and the gate would admit it. That residual\n1946|class - a complete enumeration discharged by inadequate tests - is not covered\n1947|here and is not claimed to be.\n1948|\n1949|It also cannot see an obligation stated without an RFC 2119 keyword, which is\n1950|why `unmeasured` is refused rather than admitted: the gate reports that it could\n1951|not measure the section instead of inferring that there was nothing to measure.\n1952|And the gap-quality check is a tightening rather than a proof - a sentence that\n1953|names both its section and its production declaration and still says nothing\n1954|useful is admitted, and the gate cannot decide otherwise.\n1955|\n1956|### Measured coverage of this repository\n1957|\n1958|`tracecheck` prints the ratio it measured rather than a sentence about it:\n1959|\n1960|```text\n1961|section coverage: bindings=49 full=1 partial=3 sliver=1 unevidenced=41 unmeasured=3 unowned=2 clauses_discharged=17/403\n1962|```\n1963|\n1964|Forty-nine section bindings discharge 17 of the 403 normative clauses their\n1965|sections carry. One binding is `full` (Section 6.2, whose single clause is the\n1966|native-Windows `conpty` requirement, discharged by the positive\n1967|`TestEveryPinnedReaderHasPositiveNativeWindowsAndWSL2Lanes` lanes together\n1968|with the negative `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` legacy\n1969|refusal arm), three are\n1970|`partial` (Section 14.2 at 8/9, bound to\n1971|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult), whose undischarged clause `14.2#6`\n1972|is the process exit status this repository has no binary to produce; and\n1973|Section 15.1 at 5/7 and Section 15.3 at 2/3, both bound to\n1974|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror); the three undischarged clauses there are\n1975|the RPC hello obligation `15.1#5`, the bootstrap-row sentence `15.1#6` that\n1976|binds the provider plugin rather than the host, and the hello-key and\n1977|TerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository builds no RPC\n1978|hello frame and no provider plugin, and advertises no Structured Error as a\n1979|TerminalBackend capability. The closed 16-capability admission registry in\n1980|[`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend) gates which operations\n1981|an admitted probe may confer; it is never advertised on an RPC hello path and\n1982|carries no Structured Error code, so the prohibition holds vacuously and the\n1983|clause stays undischarged. The same package carries the Section 4 lifecycle,\n1984|attach, entrypoint, replication, and historical-translation conformance\n1985|harness (`conformance.go`, exercised by `conformance_test.go`) and an\n1986|AST-derived refusal-arm inventory (`refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`) that\n1987|requires every production refusal arm to resolve to a named asserting test\n1988|in both directions, so a refusal that ships unwitnessed fails the suite),\n1989|one is\n1990|`sliver` (Section 10.3, whose chunk offset invariant is\n1991|enforced by `validateBlobDescriptor` while its two receiver clauses have no\n1992|implementation), three are `unmeasured` (Sections 7.3, 13.14.5 and 15.2, each of\n1993|which carries a gap saying why the scanner measures zero and what is missing),\n1994|and forty-one are `unevidenced`. Two sections are recorded unowned.\n1995|Assigned-scope admission therefore succeeds today for `-section 6.2` and\n1996|nothing else; every other assignment is refused with its ratio and its gap.\n1997|A `partial` binding is refused by assigned-scope admission exactly like an\n1998|`unevidenced` one: admission requires `full`.\n1999|\n2000|One admitted binding out of forty-nine covers a single clause, and it is\n2001|disclosed here rather than hidden: without Section 6.2 the admit path would only\n2002|ever be exercised synthetically. Its discharge is no longer positive-only: the\n2003|native-Windows lanes carry the positive arm and\n2004|`TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` the legacy refusal arm,\n2005|both registered against the `config-versioned-readers` acceptance case.\n2006|\n2007|That is a disclosure of the shipped state, not a target that was met.\n2008|`TestRunRefusesEveryAssignedSectionThatOnlySlivers` and\n2009|`TestVerifyAssignedSectionsRefusesEveryBindingThatOnlySlivers` pin every failing\n2010|binding with its exact measured ratio, so a section that becomes covered has to\n2011|leave those tables deliberately. Five further gaps the disclosure surfaced:\n2012|Section 15.2's code-to-exit registry is implemented in\n2013|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) and checked row by row, and\n2014|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult) now maps a failure to that exact\n2015|process status through `Emit` and `ExitStatus`, but nothing in the tree calls\n2016|`os.Exit` with it - the only `os.Exit` calls are the `exit(1)` failure paths of\n2017|`cataloggen` and `tracecheck` - so clause `14.2#6` stays undischarged until an\n2018|`ax` binary exists; Section 7.3's closed Provider Manifest exists only as a catalog\n2019|row naming its URN; Section 6.5 requires the `required_capabilities` default to\n2020|be the platform lane minimum while `internal/config/validation.go` accepts only\n2021|an empty default; Section 17.2's single clause is an unknown-event reader\n2022|obligation while its binding now names the CLI Result machine reader `Read`,\n2023|which classifies one completed invocation rather than retaining any event, so it\n2024|does not discharge that clause either - an unknown error code and an inert\n2025|unknown extension are not an unknown session event, and the four numbered reader\n2026|rules that binding does implement carry no RFC 2119 keyword and are invisible to\n2027|the clause scanner; and Section 2.1's single clause is a replica runtime\n2028|obligation that no code here implements.\n2029|\n2030|Successful output reports ownership inventory counts and the measured coverage\n2031|ratio only. The gate does not mutate repository or product state, add an `ax`\n2032|command or `doctor` result, or claim that any catalog capability is available,\n2033|enabled, or supported.\n2034|\n2035|## Managed Skills\n2036|\n2037|`Skillfile.json` targets the Curator-standard `claude_code` and `codex_cli`\n2038|agent adapters and pins this project-local skill to an exact revision:\n2039|\n2040|| Skill | Revision |\n2041|| --- | --- |\n2042|| `relux-works/skill-go-testing-tools` | `90c1515239eed9321068f3bafbeb5d0a0c2aa26a` |\n2043|\n2044|Project management is intentionally global. The repository does not declare or\n2045|install `project-management`; development uses the globally installed skill\n2046|and `task-board` CLI.\n2047|\n2048|Curator owns `.agents/`, `.claude/skills/`, and `.codex/skills/`. Do not edit\n2049|their generated contents directly; change `Skillfile.json` and rerun Curator.\n(more lines below)"}}}
