{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cabf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f78-0ca7-7650-b043-6178918d4030"},"sequence":954,"recorded_at":1780531400001903,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"09066c51-cf5e-4ab0-8fb1-8339d1838d54","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"09066c51-cf5e-4ab0-8fb1-8339d1838d54","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"09066c51-cf5e-4ab0-8fb1-8339d1838d54"},"call_id":"call_01a06f7dce817cf08ee4fa0557deb399","text":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n(699 line(s) above)\n700|- FINDING: A completeness gate over a *pattern* must also police the pattern. Deriving the expected set is not enough if the extraction rule silently excludes a whole syntactic class.\n701|- FIX: Second funnel `projectionOwnershipRefusal` (`internal/localstore/projection.go:117`) keeps the refusal decision at its call site while preserving the owner-only cause; every projection refusal rerouted through a funnel. Gate now derives two properties — funnel sites need an exercised negative path beneath `openProjection`, AND no projection-owned source may raise a refusal outside a funnel. Build-context filtering added so a platform-specific refusal is not demanded from a platform that cannot run it.\n702|- ANOMALY: I reproduced the identical bug class inside the fix. The new unrouted check sat behind `typed.Fun.(*ast.Ident)`, and `fmt.Errorf` is a `*ast.SelectorExpr`, so the exact class stayed invisible in code written specifically to catch it. First run of mutant m41 exited 0. Reading the new gate would not have found this; only the behaviour-preserving mutant did.\n703|- DECISION: Assume \"unreachable\" last, not first. One clause presumed unreachable — the non-regular branch of `ensureProjectionFileModes` — is drivable through the real production entry by replacing a sidecar with a FIFO in the post-rebuild hook. Only three clauses are genuine TOCTOU re-checks, each annotated with the earlier check that owns the reachable case.\n704|- SCOPE: `internal/localstore/projection.go`, `projection_lock_unix.go`, `projection_refusal_inventory_test.go`, new `projection_unix_test.go`, `README.md`.\n705|- STATUS: Resolved. 15 mutants, 13 red as required, 1 designed control green, 1 documented subsumed green. TASK-260830-3amrl9 rev5, handed to review.\n706|\n707|### 2113 — A gate must prove its own coverage; so must a mutation sweep\n708|- ROOT CAUSE: `requireMemberSet` was a byte-identical duplicate of `requireExactMembers`. `TestConstraintEnumerationMatchesRequireExactMembers` scanned only the latter by name, so `WorkspaceMember.*`, every Session Event payload, `Observation Event`, and `ObservationCounts` carried zero per-member enumeration rows while the README claimed a complete inventory.\n709|- FINDING: That blind spot is why a real defect reached review — `internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go` `validateTerminalV4Payload` validated `terminal_backend_id` with `requireString` only, so `CalculateObjectIdentity` attested `AX.TMUX`, `../../etc/passwd`, an embedded NUL and 5000 chars. SPEC.md:890 (§4.B) pins it to 1–128 ASCII bytes matching `[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:[.-][a-z0-9]+)*`.\n710|- FIX: Duplicate deleted, all 5 call sites collapsed onto `requireExactMembers`. Grammar enforced by `requireTerminalBackendID`. `TestRequireExactMembersIsTheOnlyClosedMemberGate` now derives every function emitting a closed-member refusal and fails unless that set is exactly `{requireExactMembers}`; the scanned file set is derived from the package directory, not a hand-written list.\n711|- ANOMALY: The mutation harness aborted mid-run on the zsh reserved variable `status`, after applying mutant 1 but before its restore. The next run took its baseline backup from that mutated tree, so all 12 mutants were behavioural no-ops against an already-red mask and every one reported KILLED for the wrong reason. Caught only because the full-repo run afterwards failed.\n712|- FIX: Harness refuses to sweep unless the baseline is green, and reports `NOT-APPLIED` for any mutant that left the tree unchanged. Re-run: 12/12 killed, 0 survivors.\n713|- DECISION: Session Event payload members are pinned by mechanical extraction from the pinned SPEC's four `Exact payload members` tables into `internal/canonicaljson/testdata/session-event-payload-members.md` (39 event types, 204 declarations) rather than hand-listed across 134 version×event shapes.\n714|- FINDING: The first extractor split on `</code>,` and silently dropped members followed by a bare `(G2)` annotation, losing `clone.planned.projection_plan_id` and `clone.failed.materialization_id`. The new derivation test caught it; review had not. Parse one `<code>` span per declaration.\n715|- NOTE: General property, applies to every derived gate — an inventory must assert that the set of constructs it scans is complete for the package, and a mutation sweep must assert its baseline is green. A gate that cannot fail when someone adds a second copy of a check is decoration, and a mutant that \"kills\" an already-red mask proves nothing.\n716|- SCOPE: `internal/canonicaljson/`, `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json`, `README.md`\n717|- STATUS: Resolved; TASK-260830-1tax26 handed to review as revision 2.\n718|\n719|### TASK-260830-1zvmw7 round-3: three unpinned arms, found by enumeration not by review\n720|- FINDING: The round-2 verdict named three survivors (S6/S7/S8), but the rework does not rely on the reviewer's list: I extracted every `mismatchf(\"...\")`/`Detail: \"...\"` string from `internal/terminalbackend/manifest.go` and counted assertions of each detail across the three terminalbackend test files. Exactly five details had zero hits: the three fixed here plus `document identity` (x2, reviewer-declared practically unreachable) and `registry unavailable` (M92 near-equivalent) — both already in the stated bounds. No other file-unique arm is unpinned.\n721|- FIX: Three table rows in `internal/terminalbackend/manifest_test.go`, no production change: `TestReconcileRefusals/static claim without manifest` (probe claims graceful_stop static while the manifest omits it; value/evidence intact so only that arm rejects), `TestEvidenceDocumentRefusals/bad platform` (`plan9`), `TestManifestDocumentRefusals/non-object claim` (string element).\n722|- EVIDENCE: Each mutant grep-anchored (count==1), vet-checked, reverted byte-identical. H1 and H2 fail with `error = <nil>` (admission, no slide); H3 fails arm-blind at `document members`, as predicted — still fail-closed, now arm-pinned. Full `go test ./...` green, package coverage 88.6% -> 88.9%.\n723|\n724|### TASK-260830-1snnef: terminal conformance harness and derived refusal-arm inventory\n725|- FINDING: Deriving the refusal arms before writing the inventory found two genuinely unwitnessed arms, not review hypotheticals: `Registry.AdmitProbe` on a nil registry (nil check first, so no fixture needed) and `ParseEvidence` on malformed `observed_at`/`expires_at` (timestamp parse precedes identity recomputation, proven by the new cases passing). Both now have tests. Seven further arms are dead by construction with the bound stated, not inferred: two `evidence canonical bytes` arms (serializes a fixed string/bool/null map; `encoding/json` and JCS cannot fail on it) and five re-parse `document timestamp` arms after an already-validated member (this leaf's three plus `checkEvidenceLiveness`'s two, pinned as exactly these five).\n726|- FINDING: The single dynamic-detail funnel is `Registration.validate` wrapping `validatePlatforms` via `err.Error()`. The inventory pins the funneled set exactly (three details, derived from the AST both ways) and allowlists plain-error construction to `validatePlatforms` and `DigestFile` only, with `DigestFile` failures asserted never-`*Error` behaviorally. A second funnel or a new plain-error refusal site is a red.\n727|- DECISION: Row resolution is detail-mention OR (entry-mention AND wire-or-verified-predicate-mention), with predicates verified from the production AST. External tests assert codes through predicates with isolating fixtures; demanding detail strings there would misdescribe the battery. Misattribution (right detail, wrong test) remains a review finding — three such rows were caught by reading the generated table, not by the gate.\n728|- EVIDENCE: 8 copy-aside mutants, each grep-confirmed present and restored `cmp`-clean: M1 replays the reviewer's exact attack (new arm, new detail) and fails forward naming the arm plus reverse on the count; M2 reuses an existing detail in a new function and fails on the function key; M3/M4/M7 narrow rather than delete and fail at `error = <nil>`; M5 (deleted relay refusal) fails the gate and both inventory directions via the stale row; M6 (swapped legacy map) fails three translation tests; M9 (deleted table row) fails forward plus the bijection. 8/8 killed, 0 survivors.\n729|- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/conformance.go`, `conformance_test.go`, `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (new); `manifest_test.go` (+2 evidence-timestamp cases), `terminalbackend_test.go` (+5 wire codes); `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json` (+`terminal-lifecycle-conformance` acceptance case, 75->76), `traceability.go` (projection digest), `traceability_test.go`, `cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`, `README.md`. Section bindings untouched: still `unevidenced` with honest gaps, no clause-level claims added.\n730|- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14 packages), `-race` exit 0 (14 packages), `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0. Package coverage 90.0% statements. New files left untracked in the working tree; no commit (board checkpoints). TASK-260830-1snnef handed to review.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
